\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$\uptheta _{\uplambda } = \frac{1}{{N -\uplambda }}\sum\limits_{i = 1}^{{N -\uplambda }}\Theta (R_{i} ,R_{{i +\uplambda }} )$$\end{document}θλ=1N-λ∑i=1N-λΘ(Ri,Ri+λ)where λ (λ < N) is an integer parameter to be chosen. Let fi be the normalized occurrence frequency of amino acid i in the protein sequence. Then, a set of 20 + λ descriptors called the pseudo-amino acid composition for a protein sequence can be defines as:\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
